Z||000000||engine18||04-20-2000||01:15 AM||||I recently purchase 85 V6, I have installed a new radiator, to solve my over heating problem... But, I'm face with problem of my 85 stalling at stop signs... The idling is fine.. Before I started on the old buy a new sensor merry-go-round, I would like to ask for a little advice on this situation... The ECM is not stating any problem at this time....||||reg||9
Z||000001||tgowens||04-20-2000||01:50 AM||||I don't know a lot about them but I had the same problem - changed the engine coolant sensor and it has never stopped like that again!||||reg||7
Z||000002||Eric||04-20-2000||09:20 AM||||Check the timing.||||reg||1
Z||000003||deceler8||04-20-2000||09:23 AM||||If your GT is an automatic, try unplugging the torque converter clutch on the transmission to see if that cures the stalling problem. If it does, the solenoid is bad.||||reg||1
